  <MetaInformation>
    <Assumptions>Normal developer workstation; operating system, maintained authentication library, broker, and secure storage provide their documented protections. Full compromise of the current OS session, administrator, kernel, or broker is outside scope. Diagram roles are conceptual, not a selected platform or profile. No actual identities, credentials, or authentication runs are represented.</Assumptions>
    <Contributors>Architecture and security maintainers</Contributors>
    <ExternalDependencies>Microsoft identity platform; MSAL; host authentication broker and interaction facilities; platform-secure reusable state. SDL TM Knowledge Base (Core) 4.1.0.11, Microsoft Threat Modeling Tool 7.3.51110.1.</ExternalDependencies>
    <HighLevelSystemDescription>Delegated public-client authentication CLI. One request selects profile, account email, scopes, interaction permission, and deadline. MSAL is in-process. Azure DevOps resource access and credential-provider protocols belong to the caller, outside this model. See docs/security/threat-model.md and docs/architecture/request-lifecycle.md.</HighLevelSystemDescription>
    <Owner>Repository owner</Owner>
    <Reviewer>Independent pull-request review</Reviewer>
    <ThreatModelName>AzureAuth Unofficial V2 authentication engine</ThreatModelName>
  </MetaInformation>
  <Notes/>
  <ThreatInstances xmlns:a="http://schemas.microsoft.com/2003/10/Serialization/Arrays">
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>S2d2715ff1-282d-4116-af5f-607361fd0a4ea9ae0dd3-6999-4c6c-a99a-057dec81b96d9ad86cf2-fcc4-43dc-9c0d-ad1adda9cad3</a:Key>
