    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>T1a9870bbe-d106-4687-b515-59f5d210bf5300607525-70dd-4a0d-b890-1c3ecb157ef69ad86cf2-fcc4-43dc-9c0d-ad1adda9cad3</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
        <b:ChangedBy>Architecture review</b:ChangedBy>
        <b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>878daffd-a529-4789-883c-f6f01fdf0cd6</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>
        <b:FlowGuid>00607525-70dd-4a0d-b890-1c3ecb157ef6</b:FlowGuid>
        <b:Id>34</b:Id>
        <b:InteractionKey>a9870bbe-d106-4687-b515-59f5d210bf53:00607525-70dd-4a0d-b890-1c3ecb157ef6:9ad86cf2-fcc4-43dc-9c0d-ad1adda9cad3</b:InteractionKey>
        <b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/>
        <b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-10T05:18:09Z</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>High</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Potential Lack of Input Validation for Authentication engine + MSAL</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Tampering</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Data flowing across Request-bound completion may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to a denial of service attack against Authentication engine + MSAL or an elevation of privilege attack against Authentication engine + MSAL or an information disclosure by Authentication engine + MSAL. Failure to verify that input is as expected is a root cause of a very large number of exploitable issues. Consider all paths and the way they handle data. Verify that all input is verified for correctness using an approved list input validation approach.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Request-bound completion</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>High</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Design review only; no runtime mitigation is claimed. See docs/security/threat-model.md#tmt-analysis-and-disposition. Validate request shape and authority before acquisition, keep provider results authoritative, and validate required identity/scope postconditions. Reject mismatch or unverifiable success; do not parse access tokens to repair missing metadata. V2-REQ-011A, V2-REQ-022, V2-REQ-023, V2-REQ-027, V2-REQ-033.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>a9870bbe-d106-4687-b515-59f5d210bf53</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>Design review only; no runtime mitigation is claimed. See docs/security/threat-model.md#tmt-analysis-and-disposition. Validate request shape and authority before acquisition, keep provider results authoritative, and validate required identity/scope postconditions. Reject mismatch or unverifiable success; do not parse access tokens to repair missing metadata. V2-REQ-011A, V2-REQ-022, V2-REQ-023, V2-REQ-027, V2-REQ-033.</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>9ad86cf2-fcc4-43dc-9c0d-ad1adda9cad3</b:TargetGuid>
        <b:Title i:nil="true"/>
        <b:TypeId>T1</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
        <b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/>
        <b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/>
        <b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/>
        <b:Wide>false</b:Wide>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>R6a9870bbe-d106-4687-b515-59f5d210bf5300607525-70dd-4a0d-b890-1c3ecb157ef69ad86cf2-fcc4-43dc-9c0d-ad1adda9cad3</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
        <b:ChangedBy>Architecture review</b:ChangedBy>
        <b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>878daffd-a529-4789-883c-f6f01fdf0cd6</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>
        <b:FlowGuid>00607525-70dd-4a0d-b890-1c3ecb157ef6</b:FlowGuid>
        <b:Id>35</b:Id>
        <b:InteractionKey>a9870bbe-d106-4687-b515-59f5d210bf53:00607525-70dd-4a0d-b890-1c3ecb157ef6:9ad86cf2-fcc4-43dc-9c0d-ad1adda9cad3</b:InteractionKey>
        <b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/>
        <b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-10T05:18:09Z</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>High</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Potential Data Repudiation by Authentication engine + MSAL</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Authentication engine + MSAL claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Request-bound completion</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>High</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Design review only; no runtime mitigation is claimed. See docs/security/threat-model.md#tmt-analysis-and-disposition. The engine does not provide nonrepudiation, signed delivery receipts, or an audit ledger. Caller-visible results and sanitized diagnostics serve the accepted contract. Adding identity-rich audit retention would expand scope and undermine V2-REQ-035/V2-REQ-036; V2-REQ-034 and V2-REQ-046 still govern output and telemetry.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>a9870bbe-d106-4687-b515-59f5d210bf53</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NotApplicable</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>Design review only; no runtime mitigation is claimed. See docs/security/threat-model.md#tmt-analysis-and-disposition. The engine does not provide nonrepudiation, signed delivery receipts, or an audit ledger. Caller-visible results and sanitized diagnostics serve the accepted contract. Adding identity-rich audit retention would expand scope and undermine V2-REQ-035/V2-REQ-036; V2-REQ-034 and V2-REQ-046 still govern output and telemetry.</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>9ad86cf2-fcc4-43dc-9c0d-ad1adda9cad3</b:TargetGuid>
        <b:Title i:nil="true"/>
        <b:TypeId>R6</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
        <b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/>
        <b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/>
        <b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/>
        <b:Wide>false</b:Wide>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>I6a9870bbe-d106-4687-b515-59f5d210bf5300607525-70dd-4a0d-b890-1c3ecb157ef69ad86cf2-fcc4-43dc-9c0d-ad1adda9cad3</a:Key>
