        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Authentication engine + MSAL May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Browser / user interaction may be able to remotely execute code for Authentication engine + MSAL.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Request-bound completion</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>High</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Design review only; no runtime mitigation is claimed. See docs/security/threat-model.md#tmt-analysis-and-disposition. Use maintained dependency parsers and bounded validated application inputs, and avoid execution of request-supplied commands or arbitrary authority targets. No extra privileged service is introduced. V2-REQ-011A, V2-REQ-016, V2-REQ-032; dependency upgrade validation remains required.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>a9870bbe-d106-4687-b515-59f5d210bf53</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>Design review only; no runtime mitigation is claimed. See docs/security/threat-model.md#tmt-analysis-and-disposition. Use maintained dependency parsers and bounded validated application inputs, and avoid execution of request-supplied commands or arbitrary authority targets. No extra privileged service is introduced. V2-REQ-011A, V2-REQ-016, V2-REQ-032; dependency upgrade validation remains required.</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>9ad86cf2-fcc4-43dc-9c0d-ad1adda9cad3</b:TargetGuid>
