        <b:ModifiedAt>2026-09-10T05:18:09Z</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>High</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Spoofing of the Microsoft identity platform External Destination Entity</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Microsoft identity platform may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being sent to the attacker's target instead of Microsoft identity platform. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Trusted-authority OAuth request</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>High</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Design review only; no runtime mitigation is claimed. See docs/security/threat-model.md#tmt-analysis-and-disposition. Use the intended caller channel, trusted broker/browser integration, trusted authority, or explicitly configured telemetry destination as appropriate to this flow. No token material enters diagnostics or telemetry. V2-REQ-011A, V2-REQ-016, V2-REQ-034, V2-REQ-035, V2-REQ-046.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>9ad86cf2-fcc4-43dc-9c0d-ad1adda9cad3</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>Design review only; no runtime mitigation is claimed. See docs/security/threat-model.md#tmt-analysis-and-disposition. Use the intended caller channel, trusted broker/browser integration, trusted authority, or explicitly configured telemetry destination as appropriate to this flow. No token material enters diagnostics or telemetry. V2-REQ-011A, V2-REQ-016, V2-REQ-034, V2-REQ-035, V2-REQ-046.</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>093c7bab-4f22-47b0-b6db-abee6dc6a445</b:TargetGuid>
