        <b:Priority>High</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Spoofing the Authentication engine + MSAL Process</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Authentication engine + MSAL may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by Microsoft identity platform. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination process.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Token and provider metadata response</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>High</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>StateInformation</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Design review only; no runtime mitigation is claimed. See docs/security/threat-model.md#tmt-analysis-and-disposition. Preserve executable identity and request-owned completion channels; validate messages at the CLI/MSAL boundary. OS process isolation is a trusted dependency. V2-REQ-016, V2-REQ-025, V2-REQ-034, V2-REQ-044.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>093c7bab-4f22-47b0-b6db-abee6dc6a445</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NeedsInvestigation</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>Design review only; no runtime mitigation is claimed. See docs/security/threat-model.md#tmt-analysis-and-disposition. Preserve executable identity and request-owned completion channels; validate messages at the CLI/MSAL boundary. OS process isolation is a trusted dependency. V2-REQ-016, V2-REQ-025, V2-REQ-034, V2-REQ-044.</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>9ad86cf2-fcc4-43dc-9c0d-ad1adda9cad3</b:TargetGuid>
