      </a:ThreatType>
      <a:ThreatType>
        <a:IsExtension>false</a:IsExtension>
        <a:Category>I</a:Category>
        <a:Description>Credentials held at the server are often disclosed or tampered with and credentials stored on the client are often stolen. For server side, consider storing a salted hash of the credentials instead of storing the credentials themselves. If this is not possible due to business requirements, be sure to encrypt the credentials before storage, using an SDL-approved mechanism. For client side, if storing credentials is required, encrypt them and protect the data store in which they're stored</a:Description>
        <a:GenerationFilters>
          <a:Exclude/>
          <a:Include>source is 'GE.P' and target is 'GE.DS' and target.storesCredentials is 'Yes'</a:Include>
        </a:GenerationFilters>
        <a:Id>I24</a:Id>
